        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="note">
      Detection rate − false-alarm rate, at most. The tight bound and the certificate take each pair through empty ground,
      TV(A, B) ≤ TV(A, none) + TV(none, B), each layout certified against the same reference, since subtracting two layouts’
      motions does not remove the reference covariance; the oracle uses the difference itself, where, told the reflectivity
      and the background, it is exact. The loose certificate with the background caps every pair at
      {' '}{pctp(shMaxCert, 1)} found at 5% false alarms under the microseisms. “Signal over detection’s”: how many times the signal
      that detects the first layout is needed to tell the two apart. Shallow, bench-scale layouts in uniform rock: more
      favourable than anything claimed, and only these.
    </p>
